	Well, after lots and lots of work, I finally got Nethack 3.0j up and
running on our system here.  The game itself seemed to play perfectly,
but it soon became apparent that only the person whose (late) character
generated a bones level could access it later.  It's my understanding that
anyone should be able to access any bones level.
	The problem seems to be a simple one:  an aclget (this is UNIX) on
the bones.# file shows that the player owns the file, and only he and his
user group have access permission (and then only read and write).  What is
needed is world access permission, but I can't change the file's access
control unless it's my file.  Even if I could change the permissions, it
would be much nicer if the program would automatically do this (as it should).
	The machine is an IBM RISC/6000 running AIX UNIX.  I did a multitude
of things to get the program to compile, which I can't even begin to go into
now.  I am in NO WAY a C programmer (or even someone who understands most
computer programming jargon), so please keep any replies simple.  Actually,
it's a tribute to the skills of those who wrote Nethack that I could get it
to work at all...
	Thanks a lot in advance!

